==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{ubor|sv|la|sua sponte}}.

===Phrase===
{{head|sv|phrase|head=sua sponte}}

# {{lb|sv|archaic}} {{l|en|sua sponte}}; [[of one's own accord]]; [[spontaneously]]
#: {{syn|sv|på eget bevåg|självmant|spontant}}
#* {{quote-book|1=sv|year=1900|author=w:sv:Ninian Wærnér|title=Mina hundår i Amerika|page=171|pageurl=https://litteraturbanken.se/f%C3%B6rfattare/W%C3%A6rn%C3%A9rN/titlar/MinaHund%C3%A5rIAmerika/sida/174/faksimil|text=Affären gick briljant, och den unge läkaren fick genom dessa mystifikationer både praktik och goda inkomster, någonting, som han säkerligen icke skulle ha fått om han '''sua sponte''' slagit sig ner och börjat praktisera. Mundus vult decipi!|t=The business prospered exceedingly, and the young doctor, by means of these mystifications, acquired both practice and a handsome income — something which he most assuredly would not have obtained had he '''sua sponte''' settled down and begun to practise. Mundus vult decipi!}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=sv|date=2015-10-02|journal=w:Dagens nyheter|page=25 |pageurl=https://tidningar.kb.se/wf7j1s6710zdkq0/part/2/page/25?q=%22sua%20sponte%22|text={{...}} en dieselmotor som endast stannade '''sua sponte''' (spontant, reds anm.) framåt morgonkvisten {{...}}|t={{...}} a diesel engine that only stopped '''sua sponte''' (spontaneously, editor's note) towards the early morning {{...}}}}

====Usage notes====
* Rarely or never used in legal contexts, where synonyms are preferred instead.